@suzanne-chang The irony is we die regularly in deep sleep. Total disappearance. But there’s no problem in sleep we don’t exist to ourselves or to others. However the death you’re talking about is not your disappearance to you the consciousness but death to others. A death in which you’re not seen or not acknowledged to exist. That experience is counter the inborn instinctual need to be seen and cared for at birth. Nature has built that in at the most primal level. If you as new born were not seen or acknowledged you would not have survived. That’s why not being seen by others and not interacting with a world in which you know you exist is the death most feared.

